# Mutation cases for "the Kotlin suite runs the engine it was asked for".
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/kotlin_engine_selection.cases`.
#
# The harness is read by the tests at run time in the sense that matters here —
# it is Kotlin source compiled into the suite the selector names, so it is a
# `mutation_targets`.
#
# What these guard is the sentence a CI lane says about itself. The Kotlin arm
# runs the 226 generated machines twice, once per JVM script engine, and the
# second run is worth its minutes only while `-Psce.script.engine=quickjs` and
# "QuickJS evaluated the expressions" are the same statement.
#
# They were not, and the failure was silent in both directions. The selection
# ended in `else -> RhinoScriptEngine()`, so a misspelt engine was a green run
# of the default: measured, `-Psce.script.engine=nonexistent-engine` passed all
# 226 cases. Nothing in the suite could notice, because no generated case can
# see which engine it reached Pass on.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --features cli --test gate_registry_contract
mutation_runtime_targets scripts/gates/w3c-kotlin.sh

# ── The gate stops running the second engine ───────────────────────
#
# The shape this gate had before: a lane named for one engine, covering one
# engine, with the other reachable only by hand. It passes — it always passed
# — so the only signal that anything narrowed is the summary naming one engine
# where it used to name two.

mutation_case "the Kotlin gate covers only the default engine again" <<'PY'
edit("scripts/gates/w3c-kotlin.sh",
     "KOTLIN_ENGINES=(rhino quickjs)",
     "KOTLIN_ENGINES=(rhino)")
PY

# ── The per-engine floor stops being a floor ───────────────────────
#
# Gradle reports BUILD SUCCESSFUL for a test task it decided was UP-TO-DATE,
# so the count read from the JUnit XML is what separates a conformance result
# from a build that ran nothing. Dropping the floor for one engine leaves that
# engine's arm able to report green over an empty run.

mutation_case "an engine may report green over an empty run" <<'PY'
edit("scripts/gates/w3c-kotlin.sh",
     "    if (( cases < 200 )); then",
     "    if (( cases < 0 )); then")
PY

# ── A failing engine stops failing the gate ────────────────────────
#
# Every engine's verdict has to reach the gate's. A loop that reported each
# result and returned the last one would pass whenever the final engine passed,
# which is the engine that was already covered.

mutation_case "a failing engine is reported and then forgiven" <<'PY'
edit("scripts/gates/w3c-kotlin.sh",
     'sce_gate_fail "Kotlin conformance on $engine: $failures failure(s), $errors error(s) across $cases case(s)"',
     'sce_gate_step "Kotlin conformance on $engine: $failures failure(s), $errors error(s) across $cases case(s)"')
PY
